3 REM THE EMPTY SUBROUTINE BM5 ONWARDS CALLS, AT THE FRONT
4 REM ON PURPOSE: GOSUB RESOLVES A LINE NUMBER BY WALKING
5 REM THE PROGRAM FROM THE START (PRG_FIND), SO THE COST OF
6 REM A GOSUB GROWS WITH HOW FAR IN THE TARGET SITS. THE
7 REM PUBLISHED BM5 IS TEN LINES; THIS HARNESS IS OVER A
8 REM HUNDRED, SO A TARGET AT THE BACK WOULD MEASURE THE
9 REM SEARCH RATHER THAN THE CALL.
10 MODE 0
20 POKE $FF24,0
30 DIM T#(8)
31 DIM B#(8)
35 N=1
36 R=3
40 DIM M(5)
50 PRINT "RUGG/FELDMAN BM1-BM8 -- 3 RUNS EACH, AVERAGED"
60 PRINT
100 PRINT "BM1 EMPTY FOR LOOP  ";:GOSUB 9000
104 FOR P=1 TO R
110 FOR K=1 TO 1000
120 NEXT K
125 NEXT P
130 GOSUB 9100
200 PRINT "BM2 LOOP AND COUNT  ";:GOSUB 9000
204 FOR P=1 TO R
210 K=0
220 K=K+1
230 IF K<1000 THEN GOTO 220
235 NEXT P
240 GOSUB 9100
300 PRINT "BM3 ...AND DIVIDE   ";:GOSUB 9000
304 FOR P=1 TO R
310 K=0
320 K=K+1
330 A=K/K*K+K-K
340 IF K<1000 THEN GOTO 320
345 NEXT P
350 GOSUB 9100
400 PRINT "BM4 ...ON CONSTANTS ";:GOSUB 9000
404 FOR P=1 TO R
410 K=0
420 K=K+1
430 A=K/2*3+4-5
440 IF K<1000 THEN GOTO 420
445 NEXT P
450 GOSUB 9100
500 PRINT "BM5 ...AND A GOSUB  ";:GOSUB 9000
504 FOR P=1 TO R
510 K=0
520 K=K+1
530 A=K/2*3+4-5
540 GOSUB 2
550 IF K<1000 THEN GOTO 520
555 NEXT P
560 GOSUB 9100
600 PRINT "BM6 ...AND A LOOP   ";:GOSUB 9000
604 FOR P=1 TO R
610 K=0
620 K=K+1
630 A=K/2*3+4-5
640 GOSUB 2
650 FOR L=1 TO 5
660 NEXT L
670 IF K<1000 THEN GOTO 620
675 NEXT P
680 GOSUB 9100
700 PRINT "BM7 ...AND AN ARRAY ";:GOSUB 9000
704 FOR P=1 TO R
710 K=0
720 K=K+1
730 A=K/2*3+4-5
740 GOSUB 2
750 FOR L=1 TO 5
760 M(L)=A
770 NEXT L
780 IF K<1000 THEN GOTO 720
785 NEXT P
790 GOSUB 9100
800 PRINT "BM8 TRANSCENDENTALS ";:GOSUB 9000
804 FOR P=1 TO R
810 K=0
820 K=K+1
830 A=K^2
840 B=LOG(K)
850 C=SIN(K)
860 IF K<100 THEN GOTO 820
865 NEXT P
870 GOSUB 9100
880 GOTO 1000
9000 REM START: THE FRAME COUNTER IS THE CLOCK. 24 BITS AT
9001 REM 59.97 HZ, AND READING IT COSTS THREE PEEKS -- WHICH
9002 REM IS WHY THE "RUNNING" TEXT IS PRINTED BEFORE THIS.
9003 REM
9010 S=PEEK($FF2D)
9012 U=PEEK($FF2E)
9020 RETURN
9100 E=PEEK($FF2D)
9102 F=PEEK($FF2E)
9104 D=E-S
9106 G=F-U
9108 IF D<0 THEN D=D+256
9109 IF E<S THEN G=G-1
9110 IF G<0 THEN G=G+256
9111 T#(N)=(D+G*256)/59.97/R
9120 PRINT T#(N);" S"
9130 N=N+1
9140 RETURN
